+// One src1 cache line holds the element i0 of several adjacent dst rows, and a column stride that
+// is a multiple of 4096 maps a whole src1 row to one L1 set. A row-by-row copy then loads each src1
+// line once per row it holds, so this copies a block of one cache line of rows column by column.
